sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor AD as Admin (SPA)
  participant API as /api/billing
  participant DB as Postgres
  participant G as BillingGateway (Stripe SDK)
  participant ST as Stripe
  participant WH as /api/webhooks/stripe

  AD->>API: POST /checkout {planId: pro}
  API->>API: gateway configured? else 503 BILLING_NOT_CONFIGURED
  API->>DB: withTenant: subscription live (active, trialing, past_due, unpaid, incomplete)?
  alt already subscribed
    API-->>AD: 409 ALREADY_SUBSCRIBED → use "Manage billing" (portal)
  end
  API->>DB: read org name, stripe_customer_id, admin email
  opt no Stripe customer yet (network call OUTSIDE any transaction)
    API->>G: customers.create({name, email, metadata.orgId})
    G->>ST: POST /v1/customers
    API->>DB: UPDATE organizations SET stripe_customer_id WHERE it IS NULL, then re-read
    Note right of DB: concurrent checkouts: the first write wins, both use the stored id
  end
  API->>G: checkout.sessions.create(mode subscription, price, client_reference_id, success/cancel URLs)
  G->>ST: POST /v1/checkout/sessions
  API-->>AD: {url}
  AD->>ST: redirect to hosted Checkout, pays
  ST-->>AD: redirect /admin/billing?checkout=success (page polls GET /billing)
  ST->>WH: customer.subscription.created (signed)
  WH->>DB: plan_id = pro (see webhook flow)
  AD->>API: GET /billing → plan pro, limit 25 → "You're on Pro"
